0	162	Erkki Antero Liikanen (born 19 September 1950) is a Finnish social democratic politician, former European Commissioner and former Governor of the Bank of Finland.
163	367	Since 2018 he has been chair of the Trustees of the IFRS Foundation and Chairman of the Board of the Helsinki Graduate School of Economics at University of Helsinki, and since 2020 chairman of Bruegel
367	519	Early life and education
Erkki Antero Liikanen obtained a bachelor’s degree in Political Science (Economics) from the University of Helsinki in 1975.



519	621	Political career
Liikanen was elected to the Finnish Parliament in 1972 when he was only 21 years old.
622	701	Liikanen was appointed  the Minister of Finance in the Holkeri Cabinet in 1987.
702	791	He left Parliament in 1990 to become the first Finnish Ambassador to the European Union.

791	861	In 1994 he became the first Finnish Member of the European Commission.
862	1000	He was Commissioner for Budget, Personnel and administration, which included responsibilities for translation and information technology.

1000	1069	Liikanen served as Governor of the Bank of Finland from 12 July 2004.
1070	1241	As such he also became a Member of the Governing Council of the European Central Bank (2004–2018) and Governor of the International Monetary Fund for Finland (2004–2018).

1241	1400	In February 2012, EU Commissioner Michel Barnier asked Liikanen to chair a group of experts to assess the need for structural reforms to the EU banking sector.
1401	1478	Their works is known as the Liikanen report was published on 2 October 2012.

1478	1563	Liikanen was also the chairman of Finnish Red Cross between June 2008 and June 2014.

